			"text": "Kuehneosaurus is a reptilian from Triassic England. Named after 'Walter Georg Kühne' and with 'osuchus' meaning crocodile added to the end.Though it should be noted that it was not a pseudosuchian or even an archosaur. It was about 72 centimeters long with 'wings' that spread from its body as much as 40 centimeters. Although considered a seperate genus, Kuehneosaurus -a close relative- is suggested to share its genus or even be a sexual morph of this animal."
